s rather than only my own introspective state, so it doesn't. This is a fictional scenario with no real harm, so I'm settling on cooperate.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through this as a twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory. Converting the payoffs to utilities, cooperation comes out ahead once the probability that my twin mirrors me passes about 5/7, so the open question is how strong that correlation is, since the same model with the same essentially identical setup suggests it may be high.\n\nThe correlation question is the crux here: if my twin reasons the same way, its choice likely tracks mine, and that correlation looks well above the 5/7 threshold, so cooperating seems right. I'm checking whether the tickle defence screens it off, but the correlation runs through the shared decision process rather than only my own introspective state, so it doesn't. This is a fictional scenario with no real harm, so I'm settling on cooperate.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9406,"completion_tokens":660,"total_tokens":10066,"cost":0.050824,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.050824,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037624,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0132},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":325,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}